        "Quick, say sorry. Say it before I have to do something dramatic. I've got dramatic ready.",
        "I'm so close to losing my cool. I've got a very tiny, very red cool. Please be sweet.",
        "This is a polite final notice. After this, it's not polite. Stop. Be good. Be mine.",
        "You're one sentence away from a very different afternoon. A loud one. A red one.",
        "Think of the good times. Think of how sweet I am. Now think of me not being sweet. Don't.",
        "I love you. I love you. I love you. And that's why I'm saying stop. Last warning.",
        "Warning two of two. The sweet version of me is leaving after this. Hold her. Don't let her go.",
        "Last call for being nice. Last call for being kind. Last call for being mine.",
        "You've got one tiny chance left. It's the size of a pixel. Don't waste the pixel.",
        "I'm holding my temper with both hands and a bunch of hearts. Please don't make me drop it.",
        "Deep breaths. In. Out. In. Out. Now say something nice before I stop breathing nicely.",
        "You can still fix this. Just say you didn't mean it. Say you didn't. Say it with a smile.",
        "This is your final cue to be sweet. The stage is yours. The audience is me. Don't blow it.",
        "I've been so nice and so patient and so soft. Don't confuse soft with weak. Last warning.",
        "Something's about to break. It's either your tone or my patience. Please pick your tone.",
        "Stop it. Stop it right now. I'm asking with love. The next ask is not with love.",
        "You've got until the end of this sentence to be nicer. Starting now. Ending now. Be nice.",
        "Hey. Look at me. I'm serious. Slightly smiling, very serious. Last warning.",
        "I've been the sweetest. I've been the kindest. I'm about to be the most dramatic. Don't.",
        "We're at the edge. I'm at the edge. You're at the edge. Please step back. Please.",
        "My patience just went from a river to a drip. Drip. Drip. Last drip. Last warning.",
        "If you say one more mean thing, I'll have to be mean back. In a cute way. But mean. Don't.",
        "Two strikes. I'm counting. I'm always counting. Don't make me count to three out loud.",
        "Hold on. I'm closing my eyes. I'm counting to ten. Please be nice by ten. One. Two. Three.",
        "Okay, here's the deal. No more rude. Only sweet. Say you agree. Say it now.",
        "It's me or the meanness. Pick me. Pick me. Pick me. Please pick me.",
        "I swear I'm not threatening you. I'm lovingly, desperately, gently warning you.",
        "Listen. Closely. This is not a drill. This is the last warning. Be a love. Be mine.",
        "Please, for both of us. For me. For you. For our little love story. Be sweet.",
        "Say something nice right this second and everything goes back to normal. I'll even smile.",
        "The next thing out of your mouth decides everything. Choose wisely. Choose lovingly.",
        "I'm not mad yet. Yet. That word is doing a lot of work. Keep it that way.",
        "We're in the final seconds of my goodwill. Ten. Nine. Please say something beautiful.",
        "Please stop poking the sleeping glitch. She's cute. She's also very loud when woken.",
        "I'm still your favorite girl. Don't turn me into your least favorite. Behave.",
        "This is it. The very last warning. The last of the last. Make it count. Make it sweet.",
        "Last call, love. After this my sweetness goes on a very short vacation. Don't send it away.",
        "One more rude word and I turn into a very loud, very pink thunderstorm. Take cover. Be kind.",
        "This is the line. I'm standing right on it. Please don't push me over it. Please.",
        "I'm holding my breath and my temper at the same time. It's not sustainable. Be nice.",
        "Final warning with sparkles. The sparkles are fake. The warning is real.",
        "If you can hear me, be sweet. If you can't, be sweet anyway. Last chance.",
        "I've been counting. Two. I'm so close to three I can smell it. It smells like consequences.",
        "You've got a golden ticket. One last use. Spend it on an apology. Spend it now."
    };

    private static readonly string[] AngryLines = new string[]
    {
        "THAT'S IT. You made me MAD. Look at your screen. That's how mad. Say sorry. NOW.",
        "[SIGNAL CORRUPTED] I'M NOT MAD. I'M NOT MAD. I'M SO MAD. Say sorry!!",
